        "x1": 72.2,
        "tag": "title",
        "text": "51"
      },
      {
        "y": 24.7,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 210.8,
        "tag": "title",
        "text": "Healthcare"
      },
      {
        "y": 70.7,
        "x0": 75.1,
        "x1": 236.6,
        "tag": "title",
        "text": "A Healthcare professionals"
      },
      {
        "y": 98.9,
        "x0": 109.2,
        "x1": 300.5,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "Many professionals are trained to help people"
      },
      {
        "y": 110.9,
        "x0": 109.2,
        "x1": 285.2,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "stay healthy and to treat health problems."
      },
      {
        "y": 122.7,
        "x0": 109.2,
        "x1": 299.9,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "Primary care is provided by the doctors (also"
      },
      {
        "y": 134.7,
        "x0": 109.2,
        "x1": 310.8,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "known as physicians) or nurses who the patient"
      },
      {
        "y": 146.9,
        "x0": 109.2,
        "x1": 314.2,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "goes to first when they have a problem. This may"
      },
      {
        "y": 158.9,
        "x0": 109.2,
        "x1": 301.2,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "happen at the doctor’s surgery or, sometimes,"
      },
      {
        "y": 170.7,
        "x0": 109.2,
        "x1": 320.9,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "during a home visit. A locum is a doctor who does"
      },
      {
        "y": 182.9,
        "x0": 109.2,
        "x1": 313.3,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "the job of another doctor who is ill or on holiday."
      },
      {
        "y": 194.7,
        "x0": 109.2,
        "x1": 292,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "Most medical care, whether it is for an acute"
      },
      {
        "y": 205.8,
        "x0": 109.2,
        "x1": 298.5,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "condition1 or a chronic condition, is provided"
      },
      {
        "y": 218.7,
        "x0": 109.2,
        "x1": 315.6,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "through the primary care system. Secondary care"
      },
      {
        "y": 230.7,
        "x0": 109.2,
        "x1": 494.6,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "is provided by specialists in special clinics or hospitals. Patients are referred to a specialist by"
      },
      {
        "y": 241.8,
        "x0": 109.2,
        "x1": 492.6,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "their doctor. These may specialise, for example, in a particular organ2 or a specific age group."
      },
      {
        "y": 254.7,
        "x0": 109.2,
        "x1": 512.3,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "Specialists (what they specialise in is in brackets) include, among many others: ophthalmologists"
      },
      {
        "y": 266.7,
        "x0": 109.2,
        "x1": 495.5,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "(eyes), cardiologists (heart), psychiatrists (the mind), dermatologists (skin), gynaecologists"
      },
      {
        "y": 278.7,
        "x0": 109.2,
        "x1": 483.2,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "(women’s reproductive systems), obstetricians (pregnancy and childbirth), paediatricians"
      },
      {
        "y": 290.7,
        "x0": 109.2,
        "x1": 507.9,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "(children), and anaesthetists (anaesthesia or stopping people from feeling pain during surgery)."
      },
      {
        "y": 302.7,
        "x0": 109.2,
        "x1": 498.7,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "There are also healthcare workers who focus on what is sometimes referred to as alternative"
      },
      {
        "y": 313.8,
        "x0": 109.2,
        "x1": 468.1,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "medicine or complementary medicine3, including: acupuncturists4, chiropractors5,"
      },
      {
        "y": 325.8,
        "x0": 109.2,
        "x1": 307.2,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "homeopathic doctors6 and aromatherapists7."
      },
      {
        "y": 357.7,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 249.2,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "1 one that is severe and sudden in onset"
      },
      {
        "y": 369.7,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 237.5,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "2 part of the body, e.g. stomach, liver"
      },
      {
        "y": 381.7,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 337.6,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "3 approaches that differ from conventional western approaches"
      },
      {
        "y": 393.7,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 471.1,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "4 /ˈækjʊpʌŋktʃərɪsts/ people who treat patients by using needles at special points around the skin"
      },
      {
        "y": 405.7,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 494.9,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "5 /ˈkaɪrəʊpræktəz/ people who treat patients by pressing joints in places where two joints are connected,"
      },
      {
        "y": 418.5,
        "x0": 104.3,
        "x1": 207.2,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "e.g. the spine, or backbone"
      },
      {
        "y": 429.7,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 438.1,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "6 /ˌhəʊmiəʊˈpæθɪk/ doctors who use tiny amounts of natural substances to treat an illness"
      },
      {
        "y": 441.7,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 356.1,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "7 /əˌrəʊməˈθerəpɪsts/ therapists who use aromatic oils and massage"
      },
      {
        "y": 462.7,
        "x0": 74.7,
        "x1": 184,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "B Health systems"
      },
      {
        "y": 489.8,
        "x0": 109.2,
        "x1": 479.9,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "In Britain, healthcare1 is paid for through taxes and national insurance2 payments taken"
      },
      {
        "y": 502.9,
        "x0": 109.2,
        "x1": 480,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "directly from wages and salaries. The government decides how much will be spent on the"
      },
      {
        "y": 513.8,
        "x0": 109.2,
        "x1": 509.8,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "National Health Service3, but a lot of people feel they do not spend enough. Hospital treatment"
      },
      {
        "y": 525.8,
        "x0": 109.2,
        "x1": 475.6,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "and visits to a family doctor (or GP4) at a surgery5 or clinic6 are free, but there is often a"
      },
      {
        "y": 537.8,
        "x0": 109.2,
        "x1": 507.1,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "prescription charge7. Private healthcare is available and a large number of insurance schemes"
      },
      {
        "y": 549.8,
        "x0": 109.2,
        "x1": 269.2,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "exist to enable people to ‘go private’8."
      },
      {
        "y": 580.7,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 450.2,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "1 general expression for all of the services offered by hospitals, clinics, dentists, opticians, etc."
      },
      {
        "y": 592.7,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 412.6,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "2 tax paid by most working adults which covers the costs of healthcare for everyone"
      },
      {
        "y": 604.7,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 499.8,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "3 British name for the state-funded service that covers hospitals, clinics, dentists, etc. (often abbreviated to"
      },
      {
        "y": 615.5,
        "x0": 104.3,
        "x1": 139.4,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "the NHS)"
      },
      {
        "y": 626.7,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 385.1,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "4 doctor who looks after people’s general health (GP = general practitioner)"
      },
      {
        "y": 638.7,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 510,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "5 small centre offering primary care, run by a single GP or a group of GPs (surgery can of course also mean the"
      },
      {
        "y": 649.7,
        "x0": 104.3,
        "x1": 320.7,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "branch of medicine that involves carrying out operations)"
      },
      {
        "y": 660.7,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 405.3,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "6 centre which specialises in treating a particular condition or group of conditions"
      },
      {
        "y": 672.7,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 398.6,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "7 charge for the medication the doctor prescribes, which you pay at a pharmacy"
      },
      {
        "y": 684.7,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 201.9,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "8 choose private healthcare"
      }
    ],
